--!strict
-- World Moments (docs/REMARKABLE.md items 10 and 11): small set pieces the world performs for everyone, on every client
-- the same way. Later set pieces join this module. Client-only and visual: nothing here changes a vehicle, a race or a
-- reward. Pure rules (timings, picks, pose, counters) live in shared/WorldMomentsRules (Lune spec worldmoments_spec).
--
-- * HORN ANSWERS (item 10). The server relays every validated horn as SkyRallyRemotes.CosmeticEvent ("Horn", userId,
--   key) to every client (server/CosmeticService owns the validation; this module only listens to the same relay).
--   Within 70 studs of a landmark's bounds, 0.45 s after the honk, the nearest landmark answers (4 s cooldown each):
--     ISLAND-2 GalleonHull: foghorn and a rigging rattle      HUB-0 PlazaFountain: a 20-stud jet that splashes nearby
--     FOREST-1 GapMill: a cuckoo pops out of the cap, twice    SNOW-1 MountainLodge: the chimney puffs a smoke ring
--     SPACE-4 MonorailStation: a ding-dong chime              DINO-4 sauropod: a sleepy honk and a "z z Z"
--   Nothing tells the player. Hearing all six kinds in one session (LocalPlayer attribute HornAnswersHeard) gives the
--   toast "The world talks back (6/6)".
-- * SAUROPOD SNEEZE (item 11). server/SauropodSneeze poses the statue and sets SauropodInhaleAt / SauropodSneezeAt /
--   SauropodHatchling. Here: the inhale draws ash and embers into the nose ("AH... AH..."), the snap blasts embers and a
--   soot cloud with a honking sneeze, shakes the camera of anyone within 150 studs (0.4 at the nose) and
--   flashes a soot vignette at the screen edges (peak under two frames, ART_BAR). One race in 20 a tiny Cinderwing
--   hatchling tumbles out of the nose and flaps off squawking (4 s, then destroyed).
-- Sounds come from WorldMomentsAudio (generated by tools/vfx/upload_set.py); a missing cue plays nothing.
-- Batch 2 set pieces start from init() below, each in its own module on client/MomentKit: GalleonMoments (item 13:
-- galleon cannons, plank salute, Splashdown gull), BossRetirement (21), DuckMoments (22), MoonMonorail (25).
-- Phone budget: every emitter, sound, billboard and screen element is created once and reused; one Heartbeat
-- connection runs only while an animation is active.
-- QA (Studio): workspace.WorldMomentsTest = "<answer>" plays that answer at the nearest such landmark, ignoring reach
-- (set "" between runs); workspace.WorldMomentsDebug = true marks every landmark anchor and the sauropod nose and prints
-- the distances.
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
